  "authoring_description": "The Mockingbird Boss adapts the old How to Kill a Mockingbird Flash-animation creature, itself a violent literalization of the famous book title, into a giant mimic antagonist. In this game the bird steals songs, voices, fighting styles, and visible form while remaining one surprise behind the original; copying the surface without reaching the reason underneath is the central joke.",
  "gameplay_description": "Use as a multipart aerial boss that observes and reproduces player or NPC actions. Its copied attacks should be recognizable but imperfectly timed, leaving a small novelty gap where the player can escape or counter. Song theft, voice mimicry, dive attacks, and stolen techniques all fit the character.",
  "dialogue_hints": {
    "barks": [
      "I've learned every fighter in this hall by heart.",
      "My version of you is always one surprise behind.",
      "You can copy the form forever and never reach the why."
    ]
  },
